ury vs. Texas A&M","description":"Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews suffered a right knee injury in the second quarter of Saturday's game at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483677/vols-lose-top-receiver-matthews-knee-injury-vs-texas-am","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:54:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5086180/mateen-ibirogba","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mateen_Ibirogba"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Mateen Ibirogba","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mateen_Ibirogba","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:31Z","intro":"Mateen Ibirogba (born March 19, 2004) is an American football defensive tackle for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He previously played for the Georgetown Hoyas and the Wake Forest Demon Deacons.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Ibirogba attended Clarksburg High School located in Clarksburg, Maryland. He committed to play college football for the Georgetown Hoyas."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In two seasons at Georgetown from 2022 to 2023, Ibirogba recorded 51 tackles with 11.5 going for a loss, and four and a half sacks. After the 2023 season, he entered the NCAA transfer portal.\nIbirogba transferred to play for the Wake Forest Demon Deacons. In 2024, he played in four games and was redshirted. In 2025, Ibirogba notched 21 tackles with three and a half for loss, two sacks, a pass deflection, and a forced fumble. After the season he once again entered the transfer portal.\nIbirogba transferred to play for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He entered the 2026 season as a starter on the Red Raider defensive line. In week 7 of the 2026 season, Ibirogba notched a sack in a win over Colorado."}]}}